   "text": {
    "L1": "Governance is the way a society is run. It includes rules, services and settling disputes.",
    "L2": "A government is the body that carries out this work for people.",
    "L3": "The legislature makes laws. The executive carries them out.",
    "L4": "The judiciary interprets laws and settles disputes in courts.",
    "L5": "These powers are kept separate. This stops one person or group from having all the power.",
    "L6": "Each organ can check the others, helping prevent misuse of power.",
    "L7": "For example, a helmet rule is made, checked by officials and decided by a court when disputed.",
    "L8": "Now tap the organ that settles disputes in courts."
   },
